MITRE ATT@CK Journey


Tactic #14 = Impact


[ The Final stage of MITRE ATT@CK ]


💥 MITRE ATT&CK Tactic #14 — Impact
🎯 Goal

The adversary is trying to disrupt, destroy, manipulate, or damage systems, data, or business operations.

Think of it this way:

Collection → Gather data 📂
Exfiltration → Steal data 🌐
Impact → Cause damage 💥

Sometimes attackers don't just want to steal information—they want to stop the business from operating.


Common Impact Techniques
🔒 Encrypt files (Ransomware)
🗑️ Delete files
💾 Delete backups
💥 Wipe disks
⚙️ Stop critical services
🌐 Deface websites
✏️ Modify data
🚫 Denial of Service (DoS)
🏭 Disrupt business operations


Windows Event IDs & Telemetry

There is no single Event ID that says "Impact."

SOC analysts correlate multiple events.

4688 – Process Creation

Watch for suspicious tools:

vssadmin.exe
wbadmin.exe
cipher.exe
bcdedit.exe
wevtutil.exe


1102 – Audit Log Cleared

One of the biggest red flags.

Attackers often clear Windows Security logs to hide their activity.


7036 / 7040 / 7045

Service changes:

Services stopped
Services disabled
Malicious services installed


4663 – Object Access

Can indicate:

Mass file modifications
File deletions
Encryption activity (if auditing is enabled)


🚩 Red Flags
Thousands of files suddenly renamed or encrypted.
Volume Shadow Copies deleted.
Event logs cleared (1102).
Security software disabled.
Backup services stopped.
Multiple servers affected simultaneously.
Users report files cannot be opened.
Systems reboot unexpectedly.


SOC Investigation Checklist

When you suspect an Impact event, ask:

✅ What systems are affected?
✅ What process caused the impact?
✅ When did it begin?
✅ Were backups deleted?
✅ Were event logs cleared?
✅ Is ransomware involved?
✅ Which user or account initiated it?
✅ Can the affected systems be isolated immediately?
✅ Was data exfiltrated before the impact?
✅ What is the business impact?


Real-World Attack Timeline

Imagine a ransomware attack:

🎣 Phishing email delivers malware.
🖥️ Malware executes (4688).
🔑 Privileges are escalated.
🔍 Internal discovery and lateral movement occur.
📂 Sensitive data is collected.
🌐 Data is exfiltrated.
🗑️ vssadmin.exe deletes Volume Shadow Copies (4688).
📜 Security logs are cleared (1102).
🔒 Files are encrypted across the network.
🚨 Employees lose access to critical systems.

This is Impact—the attacker has caused real damage to the organization.



